35,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,The timing shows one hundred and two minutes total. The firm’s terms require someone present to tidy beforehand. It does not remove the burden.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mio,,"The calendar shows two people away most months, and one was gone all August. The kitchen mess comes from just two or three of us cooking.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Victoria,,The chat shows our fights start with reminders. The previous tenants’ permanent split left them barely speaking. I fear that silence.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,"Okay! The spray costs 2,300 yen monthly, but we buy it twice! The full clean takes 102 minutes. That’s a lot of time!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I found out that ""done"" means different things to everyone, so the room's state is unpredictable. Also, the grout gets dirty again in just eleven days.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, the calendar confirms the absence problem. @Ryuji, the firm’s terms mean we still do the prep work. It doesn’t solve the time issue.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Ryuji, exactly. If the firm needs us to tidy first, we’re still doing the work. @Victoria, that note is scary. I don’t want us to stop talking either.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, I agree. The previous tenants’ silence is a warning. We must avoid a system that isolates us.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, wait! If the firm costs 4,200 yen an hour, that’s way more than our 2,300 yen spray! We’d be broke!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Rin, the grout returning in eleven days is why I feel anxious. If we don’t agree on what ""done"" means, I can’t stop bracing myself before entering.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, the grout issue is a symptom of inconsistent standards. We need a fixed definition of ""done"" to make any schedule work.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Daisuke, I hear you. But @Rin, the 4,200 yen rate is for the office, not the firm. We need to check the actual outside quote before we panic about the cost.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, you are right. The office rate is not the firm’s quote. We must not let a single number cloud our judgment about the actual cost.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Mio, you’re right! I got confused. But 102 minutes is still huge! If we pay someone, who pays first? I need to know who is out of pocket!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Ryuji, I agree. If we define ""done"" clearly, the room won’t feel like a surprise. I just need to know what to expect.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Rin, the invoice goes to one named tenant who collects from the rest. That solves the immediate out-of-pocket worry, but the prep time remains.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Mio,,"@Rin, that’s a fair point. But if we split the cost, it’s manageable. I just want the work to match who’s actually here.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Rin, the invoice structure handles the cash flow. @Daisuke, a clear standard prevents the anxiety you described.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, so one person pays first? That’s scary! I don’t want to be stuck with the bill while everyone else waits.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"@Rin, I understand the worry. But if we agree on a clear standard, the room won’t feel like a surprise. I just need to know what to expect.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
